  "body": "I'm trying to move from SQLite to Postgres.\r\n\r\nI'm on Ubuntu 16.04\r\nInstalled synapse via APT: `matrix-synapse/unknown,now 0.25.1-1 all [installed]`\r\n\r\nI decided to move our installation to Postgres as SQLite database is responding slow for some channels. Checked the `postgres.rst` document, created the user, database and tried to run `synapse_port_db` as shown, but I'm getting the given error. The database is empty, there are no data or tables present. \r\n\r\nIt looks like a config of some sort is needed for the script to work, but there are no other arguments for `synapse_port_db`. How can I solve this problem?\r\n\r\n```\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/usr/bin/synapse_port_db\", line 465, in run\r\n    self.setup_db(sqlite_config, sqlite_engine)\r\n  File \"/usr/bin/synapse_port_db\", line 436, in setup_db\r\n    prepare_database(db_conn, database_engine, config=None)\r\n  File \"/usr/lib/python2.7/dist-packages/synapse/storage/prepare_database.py\", line 66, in prepare_database\r\n    raise UpgradeDatabaseException(\"Database needs to be upgraded\")\r\nUpgradeDatabaseException: Database needs to be upgraded\r\n```\r\n",
